{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789897451,"nonce":"q8HhetGAmUVFh5QwjGyFr0gBX4c=","title":"Lua: the table library and for-in pairs ignore metamethods","message":"table.insert, remove, concat, unpack and sort measured a table by its raw array part and moved elements in it directly, so a proxy with __len, __index and __newindex (nextvar.lua 'table library with metamethods') saw nothing, and table.remove on an empty table returned t[0] without removing it. for k, v in pairs(t) walked the positions of t whatever its metatable, so __pairs only applied when pairs was called as a value.","files":null}]}